+#### `NGIT_PRIVATE_MEMBERS_FILE`
+
+**Description:** File with further members, one npub or 64-hex pubkey per line
+**Type:** Path
+**Default:** Empty
+**Required:** No (private mode needs this or `NGIT_PRIVATE_MEMBERS`)
+
+```bash
+NGIT_PRIVATE_MEMBERS_FILE=/members/members.txt
+```
+
+For deployments whose member list lives in an external registry. The file is
+re-read on every five-second membership reconciliation and joined with
+`NGIT_PRIVATE_MEMBERS`; removing a pubkey closes its live sessions. Commas,
+whitespace and `#` comments are allowed. A missing file counts as empty. A
+file with any malformed entry is ignored with a warning and the previous set is
+kept, so a half-written file never locks members out; write it atomically
+(write a temporary file, then rename).
+
 #### `NGIT_PRIVATE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`
 
 Optional canonical external HTTP origin for private Git authentication, such
